WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So congratulations
on "The Alienist."

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is your first foray into
multi-episode television.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy it?
-I did. I really did.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was, um, one of the best
working experiences

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:12.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've ever had. It was almost
seven months in Budapest

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just working
with the best people, so...

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have
very intricate costumes.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very beautiful costumes.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They also look brutally
uncomfortable. Is that true?

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.293
-[ Laughs ] I'm sorry, Michael,
but yes, some of them were.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.630
-Yeah. Well, I don't blame
today's modern costume designer.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.068
I blame the turn of the century.
-Totally. No, but they were --

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I hesitate to even say
that they're costumes.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:40.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are real pieces
of clothing

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
that could have been worn
in 1896.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.344
You know, it was like if there
were 50 buttons down a dress,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:48.615
then they weren't, like, "snaps"
to like cheat it, you know?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-It was 50 buttons, and, um,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I became, like, I had
the same costumer

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
every day who would get me
dressed and undressed.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:00.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her name was Dora,
and the second they were like,

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.596
"Okay, Dakota, you're done."
I was like, hat off, handing it

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:06.733
to Dora. Like jacket off,
like pin off, tie off.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.668 size:78% position:39%
Like, I knew exactly
what I could take off

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just would leave
this little trail from the set

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the trailer.
Like... [ Laughs ]

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:15.909
I was taking off each piece
because it's one of those things

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you know when you have to
be in it, you're fine,

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the second that you know
that your requirement

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
is finished, it's, like, okay.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's gotta come off
right now.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, well, also you're like,
"oh, I'm a crazy person

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
dressed from
a hundred years ago."

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:33.159
-Yeah, exactly. Exactly.
-And you actually, you play

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.428
a fictional character, but based
on a real woman who was

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
the first woman who worked
in the NYPD.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Yeah.
-So that must have been

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.368
a cool person to try to embody.
-I mean, yeah.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:47.540
When I read the character, I was
so thrilled to play someone

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
who -- she was the first woman
to hold a title

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the police department.
In that clip you saw,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
she's the secretary
to the police commissioner,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:57.550
who's Theodore Roosevelt and,
um, you know, but even that's

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
not good enough for her,
you know what I mean?

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.956
She has such aspirations to even
be more than just a secretary,

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's sort of her way
into this world

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
that isn't very welcoming
to her.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to ask about this.
You have an Instagram,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
a private Instagram account.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.870
-And you brag, you're very good
at using -- you're good

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.672
at Internet stalking,
and it's so nice of you to brag

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this, 'cause a lot of
people would keep that secret.

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So what do you use --

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've, like, blown my cover
right now.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.280
-Yeah, I know, but, like,
so what do you -- how do you use

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.015
Instagram to find out --
like, 'cause you're a bit

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a detective.
You're like your character.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're getting
to the bottom of things.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:36.756
-Yes. Yes. Well, yeah.
There are times when you have to

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.892 line:92%
go deep into -- you know,

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
before, you could search
people's --

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
who they followed at the top?
-Yeah.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now you can, like, put in
the first letter,

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:48.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all the B's will come up.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.669 line:92%
-It didn't used to be that way.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:52.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
You used to have
to scroll through,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.108 line:92%
somebody follows 523 people.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like scroll
through 523 people.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.913
But sometimes that was the only
way to make connections,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, like...
-Gotcha.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.582 line:92%
What were you trying to connect?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Well...uh, you know.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:07.687
-You were like, "there's
been a murder, Instagram."

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
You know, when you just feel

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
somebody's lying to you...
-Oh, gotcha.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you've got to get down
to the bottom of it.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.794
-Oh, so you would, like, follow,
you'd say like I'm --

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
if somebody would say like,
"I'm here."

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.464 size:78% position:39%
You find a connection
and then you'd find

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
on someone else's account.
-Yeah, and I just like to know

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:25.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I meet someone, I just like
to know, like, who they...

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
are friends -- I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
It makes me sound
like a big creep but --

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, like a --
like a little one.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like a small creep.
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:36.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this -- you are not
a huge sports fan,

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:39.285
but you come from a family --
-I can't say that in public.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.887
-Okay, gotcha.
-Because my mom will, like, have

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
my head if you say that
about me.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:44.224 line:92%
-Well, would your mom admit

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are less of a sports fan
than her?

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:48.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You all are less of
sports fans than my mom.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:50.230
-Gotcha.
-Everyone in this room combined

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.764 size:88% position:44%
is less of a sports fan.
-And is it -- it's been

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
problematic --
her thirst for sports --

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is so funny. So, um...
I'm cutting you off

00:03:57.637 --> 00:03:58.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
and telling my story.
-No, no, please.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Go for it. [ Laughs ]

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:05.845
-I went to the SAG Awards
recently, and I presented,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:10.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got to wear
this beautiful dress, and I --

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:13.686
a few weeks ago, I wanted my mom
to come to a fitting of it

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause my mom -- she loves
clothes and fashion.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:19.559
She has a great eye, and I like
her to come with me sometimes

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the fittings.
And so I had a fitting,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:26.332
and I was like, "oh, we have to
be at Samantha's at 1

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.568
for that dress fitting."
She's like, "okay, okay."

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:33.006
You know, that day rolls around,
and she's like... [ Sighs ]

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:37.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Dakota, that is
the Georgia-Alabama game."

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like, yeah. Okay.
Like, I gotta --

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.282
I'm here for, like, a day.
I have to do it that day.

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:48.321
She's, like, "who would plan
anything today at 1 P.M.?"

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:52.325 line:92%
She was, like, mad at me.

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:53.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like actually mad.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like, "there's nothing
I can do. I...

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
It has to be this day."
So she didn't come.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:58.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:01.334
That's great. And I guarantee
the people at that fitting

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.103
also did not know it was
the Alabama-Georgia game.

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They didn't.
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations...
-Thank you.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...so much on the show.
It's lovely having you here.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
-Dakota Fanning, everybody.

